            <ArticleTitle>[Rupture of the medio-patellar plica. One of the many causes of anterior knee pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1069-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anterior knee pain is a common syndrome in orthopedic practice. The origin is often obscure, and the attitude towards operative procedures should be reserved. In selected cases arthroscopy is indicated. I describe a patient with rupture of the mediopatellar plica.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
